1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,821
Timeouts: the processing center never answered, so was the money taken or not?

2
00:00:04,821 --> 00:00:07,226
The simplest way is to send the debit again.

3
00:00:07,226 --> 00:00:11,892
But if the first debit did go through, the retry charges the buyer twice.

4
00:00:11,892 --> 00:00:17,130
So a timeout is treated as an unknown outcome, and the payment stays authorizing.

5
00:00:17,130 --> 00:00:23,952
A durable workflow, built on Temporal, asks the processing center for the status on a configured retry schedule.

6
00:00:23,952 --> 00:00:29,845
If the money was taken, the payment is captured, and if nothing happened, it is declined.

7
00:00:29,845 --> 00:00:35,583
If there is still no clear answer within the configured time limit, the payment goes to a manual review queue.

8
00:00:35,583 --> 00:00:40,583
A scheduled sweep also picks up any payment left stuck, so nothing is forgotten.

